repository-code: 'https://github.com/KeckObservatory/pyTomoAO'
url: 'https://keckobservatory.github.io/pyTomoAO/'
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python library for tomographic reconstruction in adaptive optics.
  pyTomoAO computes minimum-mean-square-error reconstructors from the measurements of
  several laser guide star Shack-Hartmann wavefront sensors, using a layered Von Karman
  turbulence model, and projects the reconstructed phase onto a deformable mirror. It
  provides both model-based and interaction-matrix-based reconstructors, super-resolution
  support through per-sensor lenslet rotation and offset, and optional GPU acceleration.
keywords:
  - adaptive optics
  - tomography
  - wavefront reconstruction
  - astronomy
  - laser guide star
license: MIT
